<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="008" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Finance summary authorization into one shared method</title>
    <phase>0 Removal, prerequisites and seams</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags include bff-api and auth; refactors FinanceAuthorizationFilter (.cs) with REST behaviour unchanged</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Authorization refactor on the finance filter (step 0 internal-caller rule plus per-record finance.read check) that ebilling-r1 owns semantically and many routes share</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Owns Api/Filters/FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs and the finance-summary tests; no other Group A task edits finance files or AuthorizationModule.cs</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, refactoring, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-5 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Expose the authorization that guards GET /api/finance/matters/{matterId}/summary (step 0 RequireInternalFinanceCaller plus the finance.read check on the matter) as one public method taking the request HttpContext and the matter id, returning a typed result with the same reasonCode REST uses; the filter keeps its behaviour by calling the same logic, so task 033's tool refuses exactly what REST refuses.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in endpoint filters and the eBilling authorization model (procedure-and-file-model section 5.3).</role>
  <goal>A single method (for example FinanceAuthorizationFilter.AuthorizeMatterFinanceReadAsync) evaluates step 0 and the finance.read matter check; the summary route's REST responses are unchanged; an MCP caller gets the same refusal reasonCode.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-11 prerequisite and MUST NOT (no copied authorization). The summary route (FinanceEndpoints.cs:96) is in the /api/finance group (:34-37: RequireAuthorization, RequireInternalFinanceCaller) and adds AddFinanceAuthorizationFilter("finance.read", FinanceAuthorizationFilter.MatterEntitySet, routeKey: "matterId"). FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs: EvaluateStepZeroAsync (:539, public static), FinanceStepZeroResult.Refused(reasonCode) (:174), UniformRecordNotFound (:424), FinanceAuthorizationTargets (:299). Reviews: ebilling-r1 (owner of the finance rules), unified-access-control-r2, ontology-r1.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/auth/Finance/MatterFinanceReadSharedMethodTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/contract/Api/Finance/FinanceEndpointsAuthorizationContractTests.cs (REST contract; must pass unchanged)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Finance/FinanceEndpoints.cs:34-37, :96-104, :592 (route, filters and handler; not edited unless the filter wiring must call the new method)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/FinanceSummaryService.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies/>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">The shared method is the only implementation of "may this caller read this matter's finance summary": it runs step 0 then the finance.read matter check by calling the filter's existing step-0 and record-check code paths, not a re-implementation. The filter's behaviour for every /api/finance route (not only the summary) is unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">REST responses of GET /api/finance/matters/{matterId}/summary stay byte-for-byte unchanged for internal caller allowed, external caller (step 0 refused), unreadable matter (uniform not-found) and missing data (404 "Financial Data Not Found"); FinanceEndpointsAuthorizationContractTests and FinanceStepZeroCoverageGuardTests pass unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">The typed result carries the reasonCode REST exposes for each refusal (step 0 reason codes, uniform record not-found), with no IResult/ProblemDetails, so task 033 returns it through McpToolResults.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">The method takes the request HttpContext and fails closed (UserContextRequired) when it is null or unauthenticated; step 0's "cannot read the flag → refuse" stays fail-closed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do not edit AuthorizationModule.cs (task 001 owns its comment edits in Phase 0) and do not register a new ASP.NET authorization policy; the shared rule is a method. Do not touch invoice, AP export or other finance routes' targets (EB-D-194: no invoice review in Copilot).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Every change this task makes under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ is listed in the PR with a Placement Justification that cites .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (source: spec.md 'Placement &amp; New Components'), and the PR records the publish-size delta against a fresh master build per .claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md 'BFF Publish-Size Per-Task Verification Rule': +5 MB or more needs explicit justification, 55 MB total triggers architecture review, 60 MB is a hard stop. No new HIGH CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries, and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Before each push run bash scripts/quality/check-changed-cs-format.sh origin/master and /conflict-check. CS0618 is a build error: migrate, never suppress.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-definition.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/auth/spaarke-sso-binding.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/auth/obo-flow.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/auth/oauth-scopes.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/auth-deployment-setup.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/mocking-patterns.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-008-endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-019-problemdetails.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-029-bff-publish-hygiene.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Run FinanceEndpointsAuthorizationContractTests and FinanceStepZeroCoverageGuardTests green on the unchanged code.</step>
    <step order="2">Add the shared method over the filter's existing step-0 and record-check paths; route the filter's summary-route evaluation through the same code.</step>
    <step order="3">Write MatterFinanceReadSharedMethodTests for the criteria, calling the method directly as task 033 will.</step>
    <step order="4">Run the finance contract, auth and guard suites; measure the publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="6">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the shared method can only be built by changing step 0 or the record-check behaviour for other /api/finance routes, STOP and escalate to the main session for ebilling-r1.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>notes/reuse-scan.md row "Matter finance": Api/Finance/FinanceEndpoints.cs:96 over Services/Finance/FinanceSummaryService.cs:13, "authorization in the route filters moves to a shared method"; existing public FinanceAuthorizationFilter.EvaluateStepZeroAsync (:539). CAPABILITY-INDEX: no finance-auth row (grep "Finance" .claude/patterns/CAPABILITY-INDEX.md).</existing>
    <extension>Yes, extended in place: a public method on FinanceAuthorizationFilter composes the filter's own step-0 and record checks; no new class or policy.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Task 033's tool would copy step 0 and the finance.read check (spec MUST NOT), so an external caller refused by REST could read matter finance through Copilot if the copy drifted; FR-11 acceptance ("refused with the same reasonCode") fails.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/, dotnet test, dotnet publish</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/auth/Finance/MatterFinanceReadSharedMethodTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">FinanceEndpointsAuthorizationContractTests and FinanceStepZeroCoverageGuardTests pass unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The shared method returns Allowed for an internal caller with finance.read on the matter.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an external caller (sprk_isexternal), a caller with no systemuser row, or a caller whose flag cannot be read is refused with the same step-0 reasonCode REST returns.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an internal caller without read on the matter gets the uniform record-not-found result, matching REST.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a null HttpContext or unauthenticated principal returns UserContextRequired with no Dataverse call.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The PR records the publish-size delta (total at or under 60 MB), no new HIGH CVE, and the ebilling-r1, uac-r2 and ontology-r1 reviews.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-11 prerequisite. Two adversarial-verifier passes (auth).
    Completed 2026-11-25: FinanceAuthorizationFilter.AuthorizeMatterFinanceReadAsync(HttpContext?, Guid, CancellationToken) returns MatterFinanceReadAuthorization (Outcome + REST reasonCode); the filter and the method share one private DecideAsync. Deviation: an internal non-reader gets 403 sdap.access.deny.insufficient_rights on the route (FinanceDenial.Forbidden), not the uniform 404 this POML assumed; the method matches the route. Details, placement justification and known limits: notes/008-decisions.md. Verifier passes: main session. Reviews pending: ebilling-r1, unified-access-control-r2, ontology-platform-r1.
    rework: none task 008</notes>

